-- Kirchhoff's matrix-tree theorem (1847): the spanning trees of a network are the determinant of its
-- Laplacian with one vertex's row and column struck out. Over the vertices vs, striking the first. For r
-- remaining rows the elimination makes (r−1)r(2r−1)/6 entry updates, each two products, a difference and a
-- quotient, and building the matrix reads the m lines 2r² times; deletion and contraction, which this
-- replaces, made up to 2^(m+1) − 1 calls.
kirchhoff : List Nat → List FaradayLine → Nat
kirchhoff vs ls = bareiss (vertex-count vs) (suc zero) (lap-rows ls (drop-first vs) (drop-first vs))
